cc -- Command

C compiler driver
cc [option ...] file ...

cc runs the phases of the C compiler over the files it is given and links
what they produce.  It decides what to do with each file from the letter
its name ends in: a .c file is compiled, a .s file is assembled, a .o file
is handed to the loader, and anything else is offered to the loader as a
library.

The phases are separate programs that cc execs by name.  cpp, cc0, cc1 and
cc2 are looked up on the library path, /lib:/usr/lib; as and ld on the
command path, :/bin:/usr/bin.  The C runtime startoff is asked for by the
name crts0.o, and the default library is libc.a, reached as though -lc had
been given.

The list of phases belongs to the driver, which serves more than one
machine, and is not the same as what this system installs.  What is
installed is cc0, cc1, cc2, crts0.o, libc.a and libm.a in /usr/lib, and cc,
as and ld in /usr/bin.  There is no cpp on the machine, so the pass the
driver knows by that name has no program to exec here.

The Model
This is a segmented machine and the segmented model is the default: a
pointer is a two-word segment:offset.  cc sets it for every compilation,
along with the readonly keyword the system headers use, so neither has to
be asked for.  -VSMALL asks instead for the non-segmented Z8002 model, one
word to a pointer, and clears the segmented bit; the two are one variant
slot apart and are never both set.

cc also sets, by default: -VSUVAR, -VSMEMB, -VSLCON, -VSPVAL, -VPEEP,
-VCOMM and -VPSTR.

Options
`cc -?' prints the list below and exits.

     -A              Auto edit mode
     -Bpathname      Use pathname to find substitute compiler passes
     -Dname[=value]  cpp: #define
     -E              Expand: run preprocessor to stdout
     -G              ld: suppress common/global warnings
     -Ipathname      cpp: #include search directory
     -K              Keep intermediate files
     -Lpathname      ld: library directory specification
     -Mstring        Use string as cross-compiler prefix
     -N[01ab2sdlrt]string   Rename pass with string
     -O              Optimize: run object code optimizer
     -Q              Quiet: no error or warning messages
     -S              Output assembly language
     -Uname          cpp: #undef
     -V              Verbose: report everything
     -Vvariant       Variant enable/disable, see list below
     -X              ld: remove C-generated local symbols
     -a              Do not use implicit output file name for loader
     -c              Compile only, do not load
     -d              ld: define common space
     -e name         ld: entry point specification
     -f              ld: use floating point output conversion routines
     -g              Generate debug information, same as -VDB
     -i              ld: separate i and d spaces
     -lname          ld: library specification
     -n              ld: shared instruction space
     -o name         ld: output file name
     -p              Profile: generate code to profile function calls
     -q[p012s]       Quit after specified pass
     -r              ld: retain relocation information in output
     -s              ld: strip symbol table
     -t[p012adlrt]   take specified passes from -Bdirectory
     -u name         ld: undefine name
     -v              Verbose: report everything, same as -V
     -w              ld: watch
     -x              ld: remove all local symbols from symbol table

Variant options:

     -VASM           Assembly language output, same as -S
     -VCOMM          Common data items (default)
     -VCPLUS         Ignore C++ style online //-delimited comments
     -VCPPE          Run cpp in -E mode, same as -E
     -VDB            Debug: generate debug output, same as -g
     -VFLOAT         Floating point output conversion, same as -f
     -VKEEP          Keep intermediate files, same as -K
     -VNOOPT         No optimization
     -VNOWARN        No warning messages
     -VPEEP          Peephole optimization (default)
     -VPROF          Profile: generate code to profile function calls
     -VPSTR          Pure strings (default)
     -VQUIET         No messages, same as -Q
     -VREADONLY      Recognize "readonly" keyword
     -VS             Strict: turn on all strict messages
     -VSBOOK         Strict: only constructs in K&R
     -VSCCON         Strict: constant conditional
     -VSINU          Allow struct-in-union constructs
     -VSLCON         Strict: long constant promotion (default)
     -VSMEMB         Strict: strict member checking (default)
     -VSNREG         Strict: declared register but allocated auto
     -VSPVAL         Strict: pointer value truncation (default)
     -VSRTVC         Strict: risky constructs in truth contexts
     -VSTAT          Statistics on optimization
     -VSUREG         Strict: unused registers
     -VSUVAR         Strict: unused variables (default)
     -VVERSION       Print compiler version number
     -VWIDEN         Widening of parameter or function value warning
     -VXSTAT         Write static external symbols
     -V3GRAPH        Recognize ANSI trigraphs

The driver names the i8086 and i386 model and floating-point variants --
-VSMALL, -VLARGE, -V8087, -VNDP, -VRAM, -VOMF, -V80186, -V80287, -VEMU87,
-VALIGN -- in the same table, because one driver serves several machines.
Of these only -VSMALL and -VLARGE mean anything here, as the model
selection described above; this build maps the rest onto a variant bit no
back end reads, so asking for one is accepted and ignored rather than
refused.

Files
/usr/bin/as      the assembler
/usr/bin/ld      the loader
/usr/lib/cc0     parser
/usr/lib/cc1     code generator
/usr/lib/cc2     optimizer and object writer
/usr/lib/crts0.o C runtime startoff
/usr/lib/libc.a  C library, linked unless -VLIB says otherwise
/usr/lib/libm.a  maths library, linked when -lm is given

